</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Computational cost</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We used a pod of 32 TPU v4 chips to train all models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib78" title="" class="ltx_ref">78</a>]</cite>. <a href="#A1.T2" title="In A.2 Computational cost ‣ Appendix A Experimental Details ‣ Small Batch Size Training for Language Models: When Vanilla SGD Works, and Why Gradient Accumulation Is Wasteful" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows the time for a single training run of each model as well as the total computational cost for each model. Using batch sizes 1 and 2 resulted in roughly 30-70% drop in MFU compared to using a larger batch size, depending on the model size and sequence length. In practice we do not recommend using a batch size so small that it severely degrades MFU. We only used the smallest batch sizes to scientifically study the effect of batch size.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T2" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A1.T2.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:338.1pt;height:61.7pt;vertical-align:-29.7pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-205.8pt,37.6pt) scale(0.450973618207431,0.450973618207431) ;">
<table id="A1.T2.3.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.T2.3.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T2.3.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">30M</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T2.3.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">19M<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="A1.T2.3.1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">[</span><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a><span id="A1.T2.3.1.1.3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">]</span></cite></span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.3.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T2.3.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GPT-2 (124M)</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.3.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T2.3.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GPT-3 (1.3B)</span></td>
<td id="A1.T2.3.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T2.3.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gemma3 (4B)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.3.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T2.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Accelerator</td>
<td id="A1.T2.3.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">1 TPU v4 chip</td>
<td id="A1.T2.3.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">1 TPU v4 chip</td>
<td id="A1.T2.3.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">1 TPU v4 chip</td>
<td id="A1.T2.3.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">4 TPU v4 chips</td>
<td id="A1.T2.3.1.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">4 TPU v4 chips</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.3.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T2.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Average run time</td>
<td id="A1.T2.3.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">24 min</td>
<td id="A1.T2.3.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">25 min</td>
<td id="A1.T2.3.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">7.5 hours</td>
